From 88546945518674f6ed2ee604cf4370dceadd4504 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yao Zi <ziyao@disroot.org>
Date: Wed, 1 Oct 2025 03:02:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] remoteproc: th1520: support firmware loading for E902 core

Add remoteproc support for the TH1520 E902 AON core. Program the ELF
entry address, load the ELF32 firmware into the E902 memory window, and
control the E902 core and HAD reset lines.

Adapt device_to_virt() to the current U-Boot remoteproc API and
translate E902 device addresses to the C910-visible memory alias while
preserving offsets and rejecting mappings outside the valid E902
memory window.

According to the TH1520 System User Manual E902 address map, AO_SRAM
covers 0xffef8000-0xffefffff (32 KiB) and STR_MEM covers
0xfff00000-0xfff07fff (32 KiB). These regions are contiguous and form
the 64 KiB E902 memory window used here. The corresponding C910-visible
window starts at 0xffffef8000.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Yao Zi <ziyao@disroot.org>
[Adn Elkawass: adapt device_to_virt() to U-Boot 2026.07 and fix E902
 address translation]
AI-Generated: Uses OpenAI ChatGPT
Signed-off-by: Adn Elkawass <elkawasadn@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/remoteproc/Kconfig              |  10 ++
 drivers/remoteproc/Makefile             |   1 +
 drivers/remoteproc/thead_th1520_rproc.c | 137 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 148 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/remoteproc/thead_th1520_rproc.c

